<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Per-app language, so the driver's choice is not hostage to the phone's.

    Without this the app simply follows the system locale, which is the right
    default and the wrong ceiling: a driver hired from a Gaziantep carrier may
    read Kurdish or Arabic on a handset that a previous owner set to Turkish,
    and telling him to change the whole phone's language to read one app is not
    a thing anybody does.

    Declared here, Android 13 and later list KaraHoca Takip under
    Settings > Apps > Language with these three choices. Below 13 the system
    ignores it and the app follows the phone, which is the behaviour it had
    before — no regression, just no picker.
-->
<locale-config xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <locale android:name="tr" />
    <locale android:name="ar" />
    <locale android:name="ku" />
</locale-config>
